    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1998-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Each number starts with \\(9.1234.\\) The next digit is \\(4\\) for choices \\(A\\) and \\(B,\\) \\(3\\) for \\(C,\\) \\(2\\) for \\(D,\\) and \\(1\\) for \\(E.\\)\n\nChoice \\(A\\) then terminates and is followed by zeros, while choice \\(B\\) continues with more \\(4\\)s. Thus, choice \\(B\\) is largest.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Write the repeating decimals out for a few places.",
        "Compare at the first digit where the decimals differ."
